Description: compile the static library and add-ons as position
 independent code
 The packaged makefile-engine adds -shared for TYPE=SHARED but never -fPIC,
 and x86-64 rejects non-PIC code in shared objects outright
 ("relocation R_X86_64_PC32 ... recompile with -fPIC"), so no add-on can
 link on V\OS amd64 as upstream ships its flags. The static library has to
 be PIC too because all five add-ons link it in. COMPILER_FLAGS is the
 makefile's own knob for additional compiler flags, so the six Makefiles
 that build shared or PIC objects get -fPIC there; the application Makefile
 is left alone.
Author: Numerio <b.vitruvio@gmail.com>
Forwarded: no
Origin: https://github.com/HaikuArchives/Hare

--- a/Makefile_libHare
+++ b/Makefile_libHare
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@
 DEBUGGER := TRUE
 
 #	Specify any additional compiler flags to be used.
-COMPILER_FLAGS = 
+COMPILER_FLAGS = -fPIC
 
 #	Specify any additional linker flags to be used.
 LINKER_FLAGS = 
